d strength. Let me analyze the training data patterns:\n\n**Key observations from training data:**\n\n1. **Heat treatment**: quench_temper and quenched tend to give higher strength than annealed or solution_aged\n2. **Processing route**: wrought and cast tend to outperform AM for high-strength compositions\n3. **Composition factors**: \n - Moderate Ni (4-12%) with moderate Cr (5-12%) and Mo (1-3%) tends to be favorable\n - Co additions (3-8%) help\n - High solutionizing temp (1150-1250°C) + moderate aging temp (500-700°C) + short aging time\n - High cooling rate helps for quench_temper\n - Low aging temp (450-530°C) with quench_temper often gives very high strength\n\n**Top training examples (>2000 MPa):**\n- 2395 MPa: Mn=1.45, Si=0.75, Cr=6.88, Ni=4.18, Mo=1.69, V=1.11, Co=6.70, solution_aged, wrought, sol=1110, age=584, time=36.6, cool=32\n- 2080 MPa: Cr=5.38, Ni=8.81, Mo=1.33, Co=5.00, quench_temper, wrought, sol=1232, age=525, cool=11\n- 2073 MPa: Cr=9.50, Ni=4.98, Mo=1.37, Co=5.86, quench_temper, cast, sol=1202, age=647\n- 2065 MPa: Cr=9.33, Ni=2.05, Mo=1.27, Co=5.19, solution_aged, cast, sol=1017, age=590\n- 2051 MPa: Cr=8.16, Ni=11.78, Mo=0.72, quench_temper, wrought, sol=994, age=736\n- 2041 MPa: Cr=8.51, Ni=9.02, Mo=1.72, quench_temper, wrought, sol=1218, age=489\n- 2027 MPa: Cr=4.45, Ni=5.48, Mo=1.51, Co=6.62, quench_temper, cast, sol=1093, age=496\n- 2019 MPa: Cr=8.87, Ni=3.25, Mo=1.41, Co=6.25, quench_temper, wrought, sol=1074, age=622\n- 2016 MPa: Cr=8.04, Ni=6.67, Mo=0.60, Co=3.75, quench_temper, wrought, sol=1160, age=684\n- 2009 MPa: Cr=5.66, Ni=5.06, Mo=0.21, Co=6.13, quench_temper, wrought, sol=1164, age=716\n\n**Key patterns for high strength:**\n1. quench_temper or quenched heat treatment\n2. wrought or cast route\n3. Cr ~5-12%, Ni ~3-12%, Mo ~0.5-2.5%\n4. Co ~3-8% (significant contributor)\n5. High solutionizing temp (1100-1250°C)\n6. Aging temp 450-750°C (lower tends better for quench_temper)\n7. Moderate-to-high cooling rate\n\nLet me now eval